---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
	title="Pricing · Tab"
	description="Tab's prices, in full: free to run yourself, a free hosted plan, Plus at $8 a year, and Pro at $24 a year."
>
	<h1>Pricing</h1>
	<p class="lede">A whole year of Tab Plus costs less than two months of Splitwise Pro.</p>

	<p class="note">
		<strong>Hosted plans aren't open yet.</strong> These are the prices they'll open at. How many
		bills each plan reads a month will be published here before anyone can sign up.
	</p>

	<h2>On every plan</h2>
	<ul class="plain">
		<li>Log as many expenses as you like. No daily limits.</li>
		<li>Full history, balances, and settling up.</li>
		<li>Export all your data to a spreadsheet, any time.</li>
		<li>Ask from Claude Code or Claude Desktop, on your own Claude plan.</li>
		<li>No ads. We never sell your data.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>The plans</h2>
	<div class="shelf shelf--pairs">
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Run it yourself</h3>
			<p><strong>Free, forever.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Everything Tab does, on your own computer or server. Want it to read your bills? Add your
				own AI key and pay the AI company directly.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Hosted free</h3>
			<p><strong>$0. No card needed.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Everything except bill reading, hosted by us. Want bill reading? Add your own AI key, same as
				running it yourself.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Plus</h3>
			<p><strong>$8 a year.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Tab reads your bills for you. Forward them to your own Tab address, snap a receipt, or
				upload a PDF. Have as many groups as you like (a house, a club, a trip), all on one plan.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Pro</h3>
			<p><strong>$24 a year.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				For landlords and anyone billing other households. Everything in Plus, and: see what each
				household owes you (or you owe them) in one place, pay back repair costs from there, and
				split one bill across several properties. Your households don't pay anything.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<h2>If you read a lot of bills</h2>
	<p>
		Plus and Pro read up to a set number of bills a month, sized so a busy household never gets
		close. We tell you before you reach it. If you do, bill reading pauses until next month. You can
		still type expenses in yourself, and nothing else stops.
	</p>
	<p>We never charge extra. There's no meter and no surprise bill.</p>

	<h2>Why it costs this little</h2>
	<p>
		Reading a bill with AI costs us a fraction of a cent. What actually costs money is the server,
		the email service that receives your forwarded bills, and the fee on each payment. The prices
		cover those, not a big margin. We charge once a year so that payment fee doesn't eat a small
		price.
	</p>
	<p>
		Tab is also free software. If a plan doesn't suit you, you can run the same thing yourself,
		for free, with your data.
	</p>
</Page>
